<article class="env-definition" id="0A1X">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A1X">Definition <span data-tag="0A1X">29.50.8</span>.</a> Let $\varphi $ be a rational map between two schemes $X$ and $Y$. We say $\varphi $ is <em>defined in a point $x \in X$</em> if there exists a representative $(U, f)$ of $\varphi $ with $x \in U$. The <em>domain of definition</em> of $\varphi $ is the set of all points where $\varphi $ is defined. </p>
